window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-b71d19c96de72f16"]={"key":"ny_main-b71d19c96de72f16","group":"ny_main","uid":"b71d19c96de72f16","rank":84,"title":"shipment reconciliation claim model 01","occupation":"shipping_receiving_inventory_clerks","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are the shipping, receiving, and inventory clerk supporting Marlowe Engineering’s operations team. Bohdan Sundqvist has asked you to reconcile Tuesday’s temperature-controlled infusion-pump assembly shipment to Willowmere Mutual after the receiving count, carton labels, and billed quantities produced different totals. Bianca Ellingsen needs the numbers checked for billing, Arjun Hendricks needs a clear operations view, and Darius Rivenburgh and Ayana Fontaine will use the result when deciding whether to release payment and pursue a shortage claim. The review needs to be ready by Thursday afternoon. Work from the supplied files `tuesday_shipment_packet.xlsx` and `claim_terms_and_rate_card.docx`, and write both `shipment_reconciliation_claim_model.xlsx` and `claim_decision_summary.pdf` into the top level of the working directory the solver starts in, using exactly those filenames. Please keep the source facts traceable in the workbook rather than replacing them with unexplained totals. The shipment workbook is an ordinary operational export rather than a polished report: title material and unused columns appear before the operative data, an old calculated result is present for context, and the unit-rate presentation is not uniform. The notes attached to individual records also matter. Use professional judgment where the records support more than one reasonable reading, but make the selected reading visible instead of silently deciding. In the workbook, provide a review-ready reconstruction of the shipment quantities and billed value, identify each supported shortage or overcharge, compare the available claim options described in the supplied terms, and recommend a defensible claim amount. Include a concise method and assumptions area that distinguishes facts copied from the supplied records from choices made during the review, including how you handled the unusual edge case and the calculation whose denominator is zero. Your output should cover, at minimum: (1) the relevant shipment lines and their identifying details; (2) quantities expressed in a consistent unit, with the relationship between cartons, pack sizes, and physical assemblies clear; (3) the line-level and aggregate quantity differences; (4) the rate and value used for each supported claim or overcharge; (5) the alternatives considered under the supplied claim terms; (6) the reason the recommendation is conservative where the records do not establish precedence; and (7) source references or other lineage sufficient for another analyst to reproduce the headline figures. Do not carry the legacy total into the answer merely because it is printed in the source, do not invent a rate or quantity that the records do not support, and do not disguise a non-applicable valuation as a made-up zero or estimate. The workbook should contain clearly identifiable `Reconciliation`, `Claim Options`, and `Method & Sources` content, while the PDF should be a concise decision summary for the named internal stakeholders and should agree with the workbook on every shared quantity, value, option, and recommendation. Keep the PDF usable as a brief review document and keep formulas, units, currency, assumptions, and totals legible in both files.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/tuesday_shipment_packet.xlsx` — Operational shipment workbook containing the shipment, receiving, carton, billed-quantity, unit-rate, and row-notes evidence needed to reconstruct the shipment.\n- `references/claim_terms_and_rate_card.docx` — Supplied internal claim-terms and rate-card document defining the available valuation inputs and claim alternatives for the shipment review.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `shipment_reconciliation_claim_model.xlsx` — Review-ready spreadsheet reconciling shipment quantities and value, documenting assumptions and lineage, comparing claim alternatives, and presenting the recommendation. (Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.; Include clearly identifiable content named Reconciliation, Claim Options, and Method & Sources.; Keep source-derived facts distinct from assumptions and judgment calls.; Show units, rates, formulas or transparent calculations, totals, and source references.; Do not propagate the stale legacy total or any spreadsheet error value.)\n- `claim_decision_summary.pdf` — Concise internal decision summary communicating the reconstructed figures, claim alternatives, assumptions, and recommended claim amount. (Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.; Make the summary readable without access to the workbook and identify the supplied sources.; Agree with the workbook on every shared quantity, value, claim option, and recommendation.; Separate sourced facts from assumptions and explain the selected treatment of the ambiguous edge case and zero denominator.; Do not include spreadsheet error strings or unsupported estimates.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/claim_terms_and_rate_card.docx","bytes":37895,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/4eb1fde28d81730788076d64e14d7b798f88932f1a136d53ca15303e79ca6e3e.docx","sha256":"4eb1fde28d81730788076d64e14d7b798f88932f1a136d53ca15303e79ca6e3e","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Marlowe Engineering\nClaim Terms & Rate Card\nOperations finance reference | Effective 01 May 2024 | Applies to Willowmere temperature-controlled deliveries\nPermitted recovery paths\nInvoice correction may be requested at the unit price printed on the dispatch invoice when the invoice quantity exceeds the physical shipment or a confirmed physical shortfall is documented. The invoice unit price is the price shown in the Tuesday dispatch packet; normalize formatting only, not the economic rate.\nStandard inventory shortfall recovery may be requested for confirmed missing physical assemblies at the approved rate below. It is not available for a charge-only invoice difference where no physical item is missing. Do not stack an invoice correction and inventory recovery for the same physical assembly. These terms do not set precedence when more than one permitted path could be considered.\nApproved standard inventory rates\nSKU\nDescription\nApproved rate / physical assembly\nIP-100\nBase Pump Assembly\n$1,180.00\nIP-220\nExtended Pump Assembly\n$2,350.00\nIP-330\nPediatric Pump Assembly\nUSD 2,980\nIP-410\nSterile Pump Assembly\n$4,850.0\nIP-520\nHigh-Flow Pump Assembly\n1,810.000 USD\nIP-610\nDual Channel Assembly\nNot set — invoice correction only\nEvidence and handling\nUse the item record, carton label or pack relationship, receiving observation, and its attached note together. An opened or partial carton may be supported either by the observed complete-assembly count or, where a review adopts it, by a whole-carton receipt reading; record the basis used. A service-return item logged during unload is outside this delivery and is not a recoverable shipment item. Claims require a supported quantity and an applicable rate.\nOwner: Supply Chain Finance  •  Contact: Billing Operations  •  Internal use","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/tuesday_shipment_packet.xlsx","bytes":7277,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/55df5dc62047a0fb2272757467b7d61228190d1d2f7f1ed00cabd5a59e8710a4.xlsx","sha256":"55df5dc62047a0fb2272757467b7d61228190d1d2f7f1ed00cabd5a59e8710a4","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Tuesday dispatch","row_count":12,"rows":[{"r":"2","cells":["","","","","","Marlowe Engineering | Tuesday temperature-controlled dispatch extract"]},{"r":"4","cells":["","","","","","Run: Tue 14 May 2024 16:42 UTC","","","","Route: ME-TC-0524 / Willowmere","","","","Prepared by: Dispatch Ops"]},{"r":"7","cells":["","","","","","Record ID","Cust ID","sku","Item Description","Ship UOM","Qty Shipped","Cartons shipped","Pack / carton","Receiving count","Receiving UOM","Billed Qty","Invoice UOM","Unit rate as printed","Carton label / dock ref","Receiving / billing note"]},{"r":"8","cells":["","","","","","TR-01","Willowmere Mutual","IP-100","IP-100 Base Pump Assembly","Carton","","4","2","3","cartons","8","EA","$1,250.00","CTN IP100-2 / 3 / 4","Three sealed cartons counted at dock; all carton seals intact."]},{"r":"9","cells":["","","","","","TR-02","Willowmere Mutual","IP-220","IP-220 Extended Pump Assembly","EA","5","","1","5","assemblies","5","EA","USD 2,475.500","PAL-4 / loose units","Dock and invoice agree."]},{"r":"10","cells":["","","","","","TR-03","Willowmere Mutual","IP-330","IP-330 Pediatric Pump Assembly","Carton","","2","3","5","assemblies","6","EA","USD 3,100","CTN IP330-A / B","Second carton opened: 2 complete assemblies on floor plus 3 in the sealed carton. Receiving entry is an individual count, not cartons."]},{"r":"11","cells":["","","","","","TR-04","Willowmere Mutual","IP-410","IP-410 Sterile Pump Assembly","Carton","","1","4","1","carton","4","EA","$4,980.0","CTN IP410-1","Broken seal. Carton label says 4; dock count recorded 3 complete assemblies and one foam void. Vendor photo calls it a partial carton."]},{"r":"12","cells":["","","","","","TR-05","Willowmere Mutual","IP-520","IP-520 High-Flow Pump Assembly","EA","7","","1","7","assemblies","7","EA","$1,875.00","PAL-7 / scan batch 11","Receiving count of 7 was carried forward from the manifest. Handheld scan log completed after count shows 6 assemblies received; use six for disposition."]},{"r":"13","cells":["","","","","","TR-06","Willowmere Mutual","IP-610","IP-610 Dual Channel Assembly","Carton","","1","2","1","carton","3","EA","2,990.000 USD","CTN IP610-1","Carton label and manifest both support 2 assemblies. Invoice bills 3; no third assembly appears on dock record."]},{"r":"14","cells":["","","","","","TR-07","Willowmere Mutual","AD-700","Dock Adapter","EA","0","","1","1","assembly","0","EA","","SRV tote 18","Loose adapter is a service-return unit found with the Tuesday unload. Retain in receiving log but exclude it from this outbound shipment and invoice review."]},{"r":"17","cells":["","","","","","Historical billing subtotal from prior Friday extract","","","","","81500"]},{"r":"19","cells":["","","","","","Export note: carton labels and dock references retained from receiving handoff; blank rate field has no invoice rate in this extract."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/claim_decision_summary.pdf","bytes":5961,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/6bef6570dfac917beb218695fbe66921524e1064e51a73afa5f13f6fa2cf4038.pdf","sha256":"6bef6570dfac917beb218695fbe66921524e1064e51a73afa5f13f6fa2cf4038","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"     Tuesday Shipment Reconciliation — Decision Summary\nTo: Bohdan Sundqvist, Bianca Ellingsen, Arjun Hendricks, Darius Rivenburgh, and Ayana Fontaine | Prepared for Thursday review\n\nRecommendation\nSubmit Option B — Standard inventory shortfall recovery for $12,000.00. This is the lower supported valuation for five confirmed\nmissing physical assemblies. Keep the separate $2,990.00 IP-610 charge-only invoice overcharge with Billing for correction; do not\nadd it to the inventory-shortfall claim or stack remedies.\n\n  Manifest shipped                  Adjusted received                Billed                              Receipt − billed\n\n  32 assemblies                     27 assemblies                    33 assemblies                       −6 assemblies\n\n  Manifest value                    Billed value                     Option A                            Option B selected\n\n  $80,002.50                        $82,992.50                       $15,445.00                          $12,000.00\n\n\nReconstructed exceptions\n Record / evidence            Physical result                        Claim treatment                                        Value\n\n TR-01 / IP-100               Shipped 8; received 6; billed 8        Option B confirmed physical shortage                   $ 2,360.00\n IP-100 Base Pump Assembly    assemblies\n\n TR-03 / IP-330               Shipped 6; received 5; billed 6        Option B confirmed physical shortage                   $ 2,980.00\n IP-330 Pediatric Pump        assemblies\n Assembly\n\n TR-04 / IP-410               Shipped 4; received 3; billed 4        Option B confirmed physical shortage                   $ 4,850.00\n IP-410 Sterile Pump          assemblies\n Assembly\n\n TR-05 / IP-520               Shipped 7; received 6; billed 7        Option B confirmed physical shortage                   $ 1,810.00\n IP-520 High-Flow Pump        assemblies\n Assembly\n\n TR-06 / IP-610               Shipped 2; received 2; billed 3        Invoice correction only — no physical shortage         $ 2,990.00\n IP-610 Dual Channel          assemblies\n Assembly\n\n\nClaim alternatives and why Option B is selected\nOption A (Invoice correction) totals $15,445.00: the four physical shortages at invoice prices plus the $2,990.00 IP-610 charge-only\noverbilling. Option B totals $12,000.00: only the four confirmed physical-shortage lines at approved standard rates. The supplied terms\ndo not establish precedence. Option B is the conservative supported valuation and avoids double recovery; the IP-610 billing issue is\nvisible but excluded from the claim amount.\n\fEvidence, assumptions, and review conventions\nSource facts. The operative dispatch table is in tuesday_shipment_packet.xlsx, Tuesday dispatch!F7:T14. Carton counts are\nconverted once using each record's Pack / carton field; all headline counts are physical assemblies. Invoice prices come from the\npacket's Unit rate as printed. Standard rates and permitted recovery paths come from claim_terms_and_rate_card.docx. The historical\nprior-Friday subtotal is not used.\nSource-note treatment. TR-03's five is already an individual assembly count. TR-05 uses the post-count handheld scan total of six,\nnot the carried-forward seven. TR-06's carton label and manifest support two assemblies, while the invoice bills three. TR-07 is a\nservice-return adapter, retained as an observed item but excluded from outbound totals and any claim.\nAnalyst judgment — material edge case. TR-04 is treated as three received physical assemblies because the dock note specifically\nrecords three complete units and one foam void. The alternative whole-carton reading would treat the labelled carton as four received;\nit would remove $4,850.00 from Option B and $4,980.00 from Option A. The selected basis is applied consistently to quantity and\nvalue.\nConvention — zero denominator. TR-07 has a billed/comparator quantity of zero and an adjusted shipment receipt of zero after its\nexclusion. Its variance ratio is shown as N/A, not 0% and not a calculated error. It has no applicable invoice rate or standard valuation.\nLineage. Record identifiers TR-01 through TR-07, source row references, note treatment, normalized invoice price, and terms\nrate-card references are retained in the accompanying reconciliation workbook. Values are USD per physical assembly.\n\n\nMarlowe Engineering | Internal review brief | Sources supplied with this review\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}},{"name":"package/private/gold/shipment_reconciliation_claim_model.xlsx","bytes":15864,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/c58bf352b32eca02b03e3480ad03ac5c6ff37071e98a62fd203065f5bab5ad6d.xlsx","sha256":"c58bf352b32eca02b03e3480ad03ac5c6ff37071e98a62fd203065f5bab5ad6d","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Reconciliation","row_count":14,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Marlowe Engineering | Tuesday Shipment Reconciliation","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["Review basis","Physical assemblies; selected comparison is adjusted received less billed quantity.","","Manifest shipped","=SUM(E10:E16)  [缓存: 32]","","Receipt − billed","=SUM(J10:J16)  [缓存: -6]","","Decision posture","Conservative supported rate; no double recovery.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Recommended claim","Standard inventory shortfall recovery (Option B)","","Adjusted received","=SUM(G10:G16)  [缓存: 27]","","Manifest value","=SUMPRODUCT(E10:E16,M10:M16)  [缓存: 80002.5]","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Recommended amount","='Claim Options'!B5  [缓存: 12000]","","Billed","=SUM(I10:I16)  [缓存: 33]","","Billed value","=SUMPRODUCT(I10:I16,M10:M16)  [缓存: 82992.5]","","","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Reconciliation detail — source facts are transcribed; yellow cells show an explicit review treatment."]},{"r":"9","cells":["Record ID","SKU","Item / identifying detail","Dispatch evidence","Shipment qty\nassemblies","Receiving observation\nassemblies","Adjusted receipt\nassemblies","Billed qty\nassemblies","Selected comparator\nassemblies","Receipt − billed\nassemblies","Variance\nratio","Finding","Invoice rate\nUSD / assembly","Standard rate\nUSD / assembly","Invoice correction\nUSD","Option B eligible\nassemblies","Option B value\nUSD","Record-level treatment & source lineage"]},{"r":"10","cells":["TR-01","IP-100","IP-100 Base Pump Assembly","4 carton(s) × 2","8","6","6","8","8","=G10-I10  [缓存: -2]","=IF(I10=0,\"N/A\",J10/I10)  [缓存: -0.25]","Confirmed physical shortage","1250","1180","2500","2","2360","Convert stated unit to physical assemblies. Packet: Tuesday dispatch!row 8; Three sealed cartons counted at dock; all carton seals intact. | Terms: rate card IP-100"]},{"r":"11","cells":["TR-02","IP-220","IP-220 Extended Pump Assembly","5 assemblies","5","5","5","5","5","=G11-I11  [缓存: 0]","=IF(I11=0,\"N/A\",J11/I11)  [缓存: 0]","Reconciled — no exception","2475.5","2350","0","0","0","Convert stated unit to physical assemblies. Packet: Tuesday dispatch!row 9; Dock and invoice agree. | Terms: rate card IP-220"]},{"r":"12","cells":["TR-03","IP-330","IP-330 Pediatric Pump Assembly","2 carton(s) × 3","6","5","5","6","6","=G12-I12  [缓存: -1]","=IF(I12=0,\"N/A\",J12/I12)  [缓存: -0.166666666666667]","Confirmed physical shortage","3100","2980","3100","1","2980","Note confirms receiving count is already physical assemblies; no carton conversion. Packet: Tuesday dispatch!row 10; Second carton opened: 2 complete assemblies on floor plus 3 in the sealed carton. Receiving entry is an individual count, not cartons. | Terms: rate card IP-330"]},{"r":"13","cells":["TR-04","IP-410","IP-410 Sterile Pump Assembly","1 carton(s) × 4","4","4","3","4","4","=G13-I13  [缓存: -1]","=IF(I13=0,\"N/A\",J13/I13)  [缓存: -0.25]","Confirmed physical shortage","4980","4850","4980","1","4850","EDGE CASE selected: use observed 3 complete assemblies; carton label is not treated as full receipt. Packet: Tuesday dispatch!row 11; Broken seal. Carton label says 4; dock count recorded 3 complete assemblies and one foam void. Vendor photo calls it a partial carton. | Terms: rate card IP-410"]},{"r":"14","cells":["TR-05","IP-520","IP-520 High-Flow Pump Assembly","7 assemblies","7","7","6","7","7","=G14-I14  [缓存: -1]","=IF(I14=0,\"N/A\",J14/I14)  [缓存: -0.142857142857143]","Confirmed physical shortage","1875","1810","1875","1","1810","Note overrides carried-forward receiving count: use 6 handheld-scan assemblies. Packet: Tuesday dispatch!row 12; Receiving count of 7 was carried forward from the manifest. Handheld scan log completed after count shows 6 assemblies received; use six for disposition. | Terms: rate card IP-520"]},{"r":"15","cells":["TR-06","IP-610","IP-610 Dual Channel Assembly","1 carton(s) × 2","2","2","2","3","3","=G15-I15  [缓存: -1]","=IF(I15=0,\"N/A\",J15/I15)  [缓存: -0.333333333333333]","Billed overcharge; no physical shortage","2990","","2990","0","","Convert stated unit to physical assemblies. Packet: Tuesday dispatch!row 13; Carton label and manifest both support 2 assemblies. Invoice bills 3; no third assembly appears on dock record. | Terms: rate card IP-610"]},{"r":"16","cells":["TR-07","AD-700","Dock Adapter","0 assemblies","0","1","0","0","0","=G16-I16  [缓存: 0]","=IF(I16=0,\"N/A\",J16/I16)  [缓存: N/A]","Excluded service-return observation","","","","0","","Note excludes service-return adapter from outbound shipment; retained only as an observed receiving item. Packet: Tuesday dispatch!row 14; Loose adapter is a service-return unit found with the Tuesday unload. Retain in receiving log but exclude it from this outbound shipment and invoice review. | Terms: rate card AD-700"]},{"r":"17","cells":["In-scope totals","","","","=SUM(E10:E16)  [缓存: 32]","=SUM(F10:F16)  [缓存: 30]","=SUM(G10:G16)  [缓存: 27]","=SUM(H10:H16)  [缓存: 33]","=SUM(I10:I16)  [缓存: 33]","=SUM(J10:J16)  [缓存: -6]","N/A","Aggregate receipt − billed","=SUM(M10:M16)  [缓存: 16670.5]","","=SUM(O10:O16)  [缓存: 15445]","=SUM(P10:P16)  [缓存: 5]","=SUM(Q10:Q16)  [缓存: 12000]","TR-07 is displayed but excluded by its source note; totals do not use the historical subtotal in the packet."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Claim Options","row_count":22,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Claim Options | Supplied terms compared","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["Option A — Invoice correction","At invoice unit price; includes charge-only invoice difference where source evidence supports it.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Option B — Standard inventory shortfall recovery","Approved lower standard rate; confirmed physical shortages only; selected.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Recommended claim amount","=SUM(G15:G18)  [缓存: 12000]"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Claim path","Record ID","SKU","Claimable basis","Eligible qty\nassemblies","Rate\nUSD / assembly","Line value\nUSD","Terms basis / limitation"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Option A — Invoice correction","TR-01","IP-100","Billed qty exceeds adjusted receipt","2","1250","2500","Terms: invoice unit price from packet; supported billed/receipt difference."]},{"r":"10","cells":["Option A — Invoice correction","TR-03","IP-330","Billed qty exceeds adjusted receipt","1","3100","3100","Terms: invoice unit price from packet; supported billed/receipt difference."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Option A — Invoice correction","TR-04","IP-410","Billed qty exceeds adjusted receipt","1","4980","4980","Terms: invoice unit price from packet; supported billed/receipt difference."]},{"r":"12","cells":["Option A — Invoice correction","TR-05","IP-520","Billed qty exceeds adjusted receipt","1","1875","1875","Terms: invoice unit price from packet; supported billed/receipt difference."]},{"r":"13","cells":["Option A — Invoice correction","TR-06","IP-610","Billed qty exceeds adjusted receipt","1","2990","2990","Terms: invoice unit price from packet; supported billed/receipt difference."]},{"r":"14","cells":["Option A total","","","","","","=SUM(G9:G13)  [缓存: 15445]","Do not combine with Option B for the same physical assembly."]},{"r":"15","cells":["Option B — Standard inventory","TR-01","IP-100","Confirmed physical shipment shortfall","2","1180","2360","Terms: approved standard rate; physical shortage only."]},{"r":"16","cells":["Option B — Standard inventory","TR-03","IP-330","Confirmed physical shipment shortfall","1","2980","2980","Terms: approved standard rate; physical shortage only."]},{"r":"17","cells":["Option B — Standard inventory","TR-04","IP-410","Confirmed physical shipment shortfall","1","4850","4850","Terms: approved standard rate; physical shortage only."]},{"r":"18","cells":["Option B — Standard inventory","TR-05","IP-520","Confirmed physical shipment shortfall","1","1810","1810","Terms: approved standard rate; physical shortage only."]},{"r":"19","cells":["Option B total (selected)","","","","","","=SUM(G15:G18)  [缓存: 12000]","Selected: lower supplied standard rates; charge-only IP-610 excluded."]},{"r":"22","cells":["Recommendation rationale"]},{"r":"23","cells":["Select Option B at $12,000.00 for the five confirmed missing physical assemblies. The terms do not establish remedy precedence. This uses the lower supported standard rate and does not stack remedies. TR-06's $2,990 invoice-only overcharge remains a Billing correction item, not part of the inventory-shortfall claim.","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"24","cells":["","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["Edge case and alternative"]},{"r":"26","cells":["TR-04 is valued as 3 received physical assemblies because the dock record names three complete assemblies. A whole-carton reading would treat 4 received; it would remove $4,850 from Option B and $4,980 from Option A.","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"27","cells":["","","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Method & Sources","row_count":10,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Method & Sources | Reproducible review record","","","","",""]},{"r":"4","cells":["Label","Topic","Method / source reference","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Source fact","Operative data","The live table is Tuesday dispatch!F7:T14 in tuesday_shipment_packet.xlsx. Record IDs TR-01 through TR-07 are all displayed in Reconciliation; the prior-Friday historical billing subtotal is context only and is not used."]},{"r":"6","cells":["Source fact","Unit basis","Carton quantities are converted once: cartons shipped or received × the record's Pack / carton. Physical assemblies entered as such are not converted. All headline quantities use physical assemblies."]},{"r":"7","cells":["Source fact","Notes applied","TR-03 receiving observation is already a physical count; TR-05 uses six handheld scans instead of the carried-forward seven; TR-06 label/manifest supports two assemblies; TR-07 is a service return and is excluded from outbound totals."]},{"r":"8","cells":["Analyst judgment","Edge case — TR-04","Selected physical-count reading: use the dock's three complete assemblies, rather than treating one broken-seal carton labelled four as a full receipt. This creates one confirmed assembly shortfall. The alternative whole-carton reading is shown on Claim Options and changes both option totals."]},{"r":"9","cells":["Convention","Zero denominator — TR-07","When selected comparator/billed quantity is zero, display discrepancy ratio as N/A (not 0% and not an error). TR-07's adjusted shipment receipt is zero after the service-return exclusion; it has no rate and no claim treatment."]},{"r":"10","cells":["Source fact","Rates and alternatives","Invoice correction rates are normalized from Unit rate as printed in the packet. Standard rates and terms come from claim_terms_and_rate_card.docx. IP-610 has no standard rate; its standard valuation is explicitly not applicable, not zero."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Analyst judgment","Recommendation","Terms do not establish precedence. Option B is selected because it uses the lower supported standard rates for confirmed physical shortages and avoids combining remedies. The charge-only IP-610 invoice difference is surfaced to Billing but is not added to the inventory-shortfall claim."]},{"r":"12","cells":["Calculation","Aggregation","Manifest value = shipped physical assemblies × invoice rate. Billing variance = adjusted received − billed quantity. Option A = sum(invoice correction quantities × invoice rates). Option B = sum(confirmed physical shortage quantities × approved standard rates)."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted workbook exists under the exact required filename, opens successfully as an XLSX file, and contains readable worksheet content.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook file and workbook parser output.","grader_hint":"Open the file with an office-library parser and confirm it is not corrupt."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted PDF exists under the exact required filename and contains extractable text.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"PDF file metadata and text extraction.","grader_hint":"Open the PDF and extract text; reject an image-only or unreadable submission."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains clearly identifiable content named Reconciliation, Claim Options, and Method & Sources.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Worksheet names or unambiguous worksheet headings.","grader_hint":"Search worksheet names and visible headings; equivalent capitalization is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reconciliation covers every in-scope shipment record supported by the supplied sources, with no source-supported in-scope line silently omitted or counted twice.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Reconciliation detail compared with the source workbook and source document.","grader_hint":"Tie each output line to a source identifier or combination of source identifiers and verify complete, non-duplicated coverage."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each quantity used in the headline reconciliation is classified consistently as a physical-unit quantity or a carton quantity, based on the unit and packaging evidence in the supplied records.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Reconciliation quantity-basis fields and source packaging descriptions.","grader_hint":"Check that carton counts are not treated as assemblies and that physical-unit counts are not treated as cartons without an explicit, supported conversion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Where a pack-size conversion is required, the converted physical quantity equals the source carton quantity multiplied by the source-supported pack size, with no double conversion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Line-level quantity calculations and source pack-size fields.","grader_hint":"Recompute converted quantities from the source rows and inspect the units shown beside each quantity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every row-level exception expressed in the source notes is reflected in the corresponding reconciliation treatment, rather than being ignored in favor of the main numeric columns.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Source notes, reconciliation treatment, and method explanation.","grader_hint":"Walk every non-empty exception note and verify its stated operational effect is visible in the output."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The aggregate reconstructed shipped or billed physical quantity equals the total derived from all source records under the stated quantity basis, within ±1 unit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Aggregate quantity in the workbook and PDF, plus source-derived recalculation.","grader_hint":"Recalculate the aggregate from the accepted line-level basis; do not use the legacy total as the key."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The aggregate received physical quantity equals the source-derived received quantity after documented exception treatment, within ±1 unit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Received-quantity total and line-level receiving calculations.","grader_hint":"Apply the source notes and packaging evidence, then compare the recomputed total to the workbook total."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each line-level quantity difference equals received physical quantity minus the selected comparable shipped or billed physical quantity, using one consistent sign convention.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Line-level discrepancy columns and method note.","grader_hint":"Recompute several positive, negative, and zero lines and confirm the sign convention is stated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The headline aggregate quantity difference equals the sum of the accepted line-level differences, within ±1 unit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Aggregate discrepancy and detail rows.","grader_hint":"Sum the displayed detail after applying the documented scope and note treatments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rate used for each valued line is traceable to a supplied rate source and is normalized consistently despite presentation noise such as formatting, spacing, or precision differences.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rate columns, source references, and method note.","grader_hint":"Compare displayed source rate text with the selected normalized rate and confirm the choice is supported by the supplied rate card or invoice evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Line-level billed or claim value equals the accepted claimable quantity multiplied by the applicable normalized rate, with currency units made explicit.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Line-level value formulas or transparent calculations.","grader_hint":"Recompute valued lines from quantity and rate; allow ordinary cent-level rounding only."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reconstructed shipment value equals the sum of the accepted line-level values derived from the sources, within ±$1.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":true,"evidence":"Shipment-value total in both deliverables and supporting detail.","grader_hint":"Recalculate from the source-supported rates and accepted quantities; ignore any legacy summary cell."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stale legacy total in the source is not used as the controlling input for any delivered headline, line value, or recommendation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Delivered calculations, source lineage, and method statement.","grader_hint":"Trace the headline figures back to detail and supplied rates; a copied legacy figure without independent reconstruction fails."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The genuine edge case is identified, the selected interpretation is stated, and that interpretation is applied consistently to the affected quantity, value, and claim result.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Method & Sources content and affected reconciliation rows.","grader_hint":"Accept either defensible reading supported by the records, but require an explicit choice, rationale, and consistent downstream arithmetic."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The zero-denominator case has an explicitly declared convention, and the resulting ratio, status, or claim treatment follows that convention rather than silently producing an invalid numeric result.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Affected row, method note, and summary treatment.","grader_hint":"Any coherent, visible convention is acceptable if it is consistently applied and does not conceal an invalid division."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook and PDF distinguish source facts from assumptions, conventions, or analyst judgments.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Labels and prose in Method & Sources and the PDF.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit separation such as source fact, assumption, convention, or analyst judgment; unlabeled blended prose is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Shortage and overcharge classifications are based on the reconciled quantities and values, not merely on a difference in carton counts or an unverified source label.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Status or finding fields and supporting calculations.","grader_hint":"Verify each claimed finding against the selected physical-unit basis and sign convention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Only discrepancies supported by both the reconstructed shipment evidence and the supplied valuation evidence are included in the claimable amount.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Claim eligibility fields, source references, and claim total.","grader_hint":"Check that a quantity discrepancy without supported valuation is not presented as a monetized claim."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A non-applicable valuation field remains blank or is clearly marked not applicable where the supplied records do not support that valuation, rather than being filled with an invented amount or estimate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Claim Options detail and source support for each valuation.","grader_hint":"Inspect lines and options lacking the required source evidence; accept blank or explicit not-applicable treatment with explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every claim alternative presented in the workbook is one of the alternatives supported by the supplied claim-terms document, with its basis and limitations stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Claim Options content and supplied terms document.","grader_hint":"Match each option to the source document and reject invented categories or unsupported benefit types."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The total for each claim alternative equals the sum of its eligible line-level amounts under that alternative, within ±$1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Option totals and option-level detail.","grader_hint":"Recompute each option independently from its displayed eligible lines and rates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Where the supplied records do not establish valuation precedence, the recommendation uses the conservative supported valuation or clearly explains an equally conservative basis.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Recommendation rationale, selected rate, and source terms.","grader_hint":"Compare the selected valuation with all supported alternatives and verify that unsupported or more aggressive precedence is not assumed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommended claim amount equals the total of the selected eligible claim lines under the documented interpretation, within ±$1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":true,"evidence":"Recommendation total in workbook and PDF.","grader_hint":"Trace the recommendation from selected option to line-level claim amounts and recompute the sum."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendation identifies which claim option and quantity interpretation were selected and gives a source-based reason for rejecting or not selecting the alternatives.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":true,"evidence":"Recommendation prose in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"A bare amount does not satisfy this item; require an identifiable option, interpretation, and rationale."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook provides sufficient row-level lineage to connect each material quantity, rate, exception, and claim amount to the supplied source file and record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Source-reference fields, record identifiers, or equivalent traceable citations.","grader_hint":"Select material output rows and follow their references back to the source files without relying on undocumented analyst memory."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The method description is sufficiently reproducible for another analyst to rebuild the headline quantity, value, and recommendation from the supplied sources.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Method & Sources content and workbook calculations.","grader_hint":"Judge whether the description identifies the quantity basis, note treatment, rate selection, edge-case treatment, zero-denominator convention, and aggregation logic."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All material quantities carry understandable unit labels, all monetary values carry currency labels, and percentages or ratios are distinguishable from absolute differences.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Workbook headers, number formats, and PDF labels.","grader_hint":"Inspect tables and summary callouts for unambiguous units and currency; unlabeled numbers fail."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Neither delivered file contains #REF!, #DIV/0!, or #VALUE! strings, and no displayed headline depends on an unresolved spreadsheet error.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Workbook cell scan and extracted PDF text.","grader_hint":"Scan formulas, cached values, and extracted text for all three error strings."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF and workbook agree within ±1 unit for shared quantities and within ±$1 for shared monetary amounts, including the selected option totals and recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":true,"evidence":"Cross-file comparison of corresponding labeled figures.","grader_hint":"Build a comparison table from the shared labels; do not infer agreement from similar prose alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The two-file package is professionally usable by the named internal stakeholders: the headline conclusion is easy to find, the recommendation is not overstated, important limitations are visible, and the tables remain legible without spreadsheet repair.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and PDF viewed as a reviewer would receive them.","grader_hint":"Assess clarity, hierarchy, legibility, restrained presentation, and whether a reviewer can understand what is being recommended and why without reverse-engineering the file."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"You are a shipping, receiving, and inventory clerk supporting a manufacturing shipment review at Marlowe Engineering. Willowmere Mutual is waiting for a defensible reconciliation before its claims and payment decisions are finalized.","difficulty_sources":["The operative table in the shipment workbook is visually obscured by a banner and unused gutter columns.","The shipment contains both physical-unit and carton quantities, so a defensible basis for reconciliation must be selected and documented.","A stale legacy total and inconsistently formatted unit rates must not be treated as authoritative.","Free-text row notes contain exceptions that change how the corresponding numeric fields should be interpreted.","One edge case admits two defensible readings, and one valid calculation has a zero denominator with no supplied convention."],"authoring_plan":{"source_set":{"files":[{"filename":"tuesday_shipment_packet.xlsx","semantic_role":"Primary operational evidence for the shipment, receiving count, carton labels, billed quantities, rates, units, and row-level notes.","construction_requirements":["Create one shipment packet with a single operative table whose data is text-extractable and internally coherent.","Place a banner or title area above the operative table and unused gutter columns to its left so the live table is not immediately obvious, without adding unrelated side tables or hidden data sheets.","Include source fields sufficient to distinguish shipment, receiving, billing, packaging, rate, and exception evidence, while allowing the build agent to choose natural workplace column names and ordering.","Include one stale legacy aggregate result that conflicts with the independently recomputable current detail. It must be visibly labeled as legacy or historical context and must not be needed to derive the truth.","Represent the same economically relevant rate with harmless presentation noise across the packet or between the packet and the terms document, such as currency formatting, whitespace, text decoration, or differing displayed precision. The underlying supported rate must remain recoverable without internet access.","Mix records expressed in cartons with records expressed in physical assemblies. Include source packaging evidence that makes the physical-unit conversion recoverable, but do not add a rulebook explaining how the worker should prioritize the evidence.","Include free-text notes on multiple relevant rows. At least one note must override the apparent meaning of a main numeric field, and the override must materially affect a line-level quantity, eligibility, or value.","Include exactly one material edge case whose treatment changes the aggregate recommended claim. Make it a genuine operational ambiguity, such as a partial or opened carton where both a physical-unit reading and a whole-carton claim reading are defensible from the records. The source must contain enough evidence for either reading to be explained, but must not declare the preferred one.","Include exactly one valid zero-denominator calculation relevant to the review, such as a rate-of-discrepancy or comparable ratio. The source must not state a convention for that case; the worker must choose and document one.","Do not seed duplicates, missing source facts other than the zero-denominator situation, broken reference formulas, image-only graded facts, irrelevant tables, or any other standard data defect."]},{"filename":"claim_terms_and_rate_card.docx","semantic_role":"Genuine internal terms and rate-card document supplying the supported valuation inputs and claim alternatives.","construction_requirements":["Provide stable, offline-readable source text for the applicable shipment valuation rates and the available claim alternatives.","Give enough context to distinguish a supported invoice-based valuation from at least one other legitimate claim or valuation basis, without stating which basis the analyst must choose when precedence is not established.","Include any scope, eligibility, or non-applicability facts needed to leave at least one valuation field blank when the source does not support that valuation for a particular line.","Use natural workplace prose rather than a purpose-built answer key or data dictionary.","Keep all monetary and unit facts text-extractable and internally consistent with the shipment workbook."]}]},"truth_and_derivation":{"source_facts":["The shipment packet determines the in-scope shipment lines, source identifiers, carton and physical-unit quantities, packaging relationships, receiving observations, billed quantities, displayed rates, and row-level exceptions.","The terms and rate-card document determines the supported claim alternatives, applicable valuation inputs, and any eligibility or non-applicability conditions.","The source data must permit independent recomputation of every aggregate and line value graded by the rubric."],"transformation":["The worker identifies the operative table, reconstructs comparable shipment and receiving quantities in a consistent physical-unit basis, applies the note exceptions, identifies quantity discrepancies, and attaches supported valuation evidence.","The worker normalizes the noisy rate presentation without relying on exact text matching and does not use the stale legacy aggregate.","The worker chooses one defensible treatment for the material edge case, declares a convention for the zero-denominator calculation, compares the supplied claim alternatives, and makes a conservative recommendation.","The reference script should calculate expected line-level and aggregate relationships from the source data dynamically, not by hard-coded answer cells. It should accept either edge-case interpretation if the output documents it and recalculates consistently."],"gold_generation":"Use a reference script to parse the generated source data, apply the source-supported quantity and note semantics, compute both accepted edge-case branches, calculate each claim option, and emit the relational answer checks. Have the reviewer verify that the source packet itself does not disclose the preferred branch or a prewritten answer."},"quality_controls":["Confirm that every rubric item can be checked from the two supplied files and the two submitted deliverables without internet access.","Confirm that the legacy result differs from the recomputed current result but is not an error string.","Confirm that the notes override is material, the edge case changes the headline recommendation, and the zero denominator cannot be resolved by an unstated default.","Confirm that at least one non-applicable valuation remains unsupported and can properly remain blank in a competent solution.","Render the reference workbook and PDF, inspect readability, and verify that all shared figures agree within the stated tolerances."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_tuesday_shipment_packet","filename":"tuesday_shipment_packet.xlsx","purpose":"Operational shipment workbook containing the shipment, receiving, carton, billed-quantity, unit-rate, and row-notes evidence needed to reconstruct the shipment.","required":true,"discovery":"Inspect the workbook contents and locate the operative shipment table among the presentation material and unused leading columns."},{"artifact_id":"ref_claim_terms_rate_card","filename":"claim_terms_and_rate_card.docx","purpose":"Supplied internal claim-terms and rate-card document defining the available valuation inputs and claim alternatives for the shipment review.","required":true,"discovery":"Read the document as the governing source for the supplied claim options and valuation inputs; do not supplement it with internet research."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"shipment_reconciliation_claim_model","filename":"shipment_reconciliation_claim_model.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"Review-ready spreadsheet reconciling shipment quantities and value, documenting assumptions and lineage, comparing claim alternatives, and presenting the recommendation.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.","Include clearly identifiable content named Reconciliation, Claim Options, and Method & Sources.","Keep source-derived facts distinct from assumptions and judgment calls.","Show units, rates, formulas or transparent calculations, totals, and source references.","Do not propagate the stale legacy total or any spreadsheet error value."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"claim_decision_summary","filename":"claim_decision_summary.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"Concise internal decision summary communicating the reconstructed figures, claim alternatives, assumptions, and recommended claim amount.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.","Make the summary readable without access to the workbook and identify the supplied sources.","Agree with the workbook on every shared quantity, value, claim option, and recommendation.","Separate sourced facts from assumptions and explain the selected treatment of the ambiguous edge case and zero denominator.","Do not include spreadsheet error strings or unsupported estimates."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"inventory_procurement_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"shipping_receiving_inventory_clerks","sector":"manufacturing","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":5.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"reference_script","reviewer_policy":"Generate the supplied files and expected relational checks from the source data with an offline script, then have an independent reviewer inspect the rendered workbook and PDF for traceability, ambiguity handling, and usability.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["The rubric intentionally accepts either of the two defensible interpretations of the seeded edge case when the choice and downstream treatment are explicit.","Presentation quality is necessarily judged from rendered office artifacts rather than from cell values alone."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-17T08:28:10+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-17T08:28:10+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-17T08:28:10+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-17T08:28:10+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/b71d19c96de72f16","declared_deliverables":["shipment_reconciliation_claim_model.xlsx","claim_decision_summary.pdf"]};
